    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="15">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 15</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ Sunnandaga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#ICn_15.lnote.oe.27"/> cypingce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#ICn_15.lnote.oe.25"/> we forbeodað eac eornostlice ⁊ ælc folcgemot, butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_15.lnote.oe.1"/> hit for micelre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_15.lnote.oe.2"/> neodþearfe sig.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_15.lnote.oe.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>And Sunnandæga cypingce we forbeodað eac eornostlice ⁊ ælc folcgemot, buton hit for mycelre neodþearfe sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>Ipsa uero die Dominica publica mercimonia uel placitationum conuenticula, uenationes et huiusmodi secularium actiones<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_15.lnote.oe.1-2"/> exerceri modis omnibus prohibemus, nisi pro magna necessitate sit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ Sunnandæges cypinge we forbeodað eac eornostlice ⁊ ælc folcgemót, buton hit for mycelre nydðearfe sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="295" ed="#liebermann"/>Interdicimus etiam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#ICn_15.lnote.oe.30"/> mercatum dierum Dominicorum et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#ICn_15.lnote.oe.31"/> omnia popularia<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_15.lnote.oe.1-3"/> placita, nisi maxima<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_15.lnote.oe.2-2"/> sit necessitas.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="295" ed="#liebermann"/>Interdicimus etiam diligenter diei Dominice mercacionem et omnem uulgi placitacionem, nisi necessitas arta coegerit,</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="15" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="166" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ Sunnandæges<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#ICn_15.robnote.fn.4"/> cypinge we forbeodað eac eornostlice ⁊ ælc folcgemót, buton hit for mycelre nydðearfe sy.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="244" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And Sunnandaga cypingce we forbeodað eac eornostlice and ælc folcgemot, butan hit for micelre neodþearfe sig.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="295" ed="#liebermann"/>Und Kaufgeschäft der Sonntage<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_15.lnote.de.1"/> (Sonntags <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) verbieten wir ebenfalls ernstlich und jede Volksversammlung [zum Gericht], ausser wenn es aus grossem Nothwendigkeitszwange geschieht.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And trading on Sundays (on Sunday, B) we also strictly forbid, and every public assembly [for justice], unless it is for great necessity.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_15.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="167" ed="#robertson"/>And likewise we strictly forbid Sunday trade and all public gatherings, unless in cases of great necessity.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="245" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And we also prohibit most strictly the transaction of business on Sundays and all public meetings, unless there is a great need for one.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="295, 296"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_22-1">VI Atr 22.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. VI Atr. 22, 1 | VI Atr. 22, 1</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Northu_55">Northu 55</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_22-1">VI Atr 22.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 15-15:1: Cn 1018:14:1  VI Atr 22:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-039">Cn 1018 14.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 15-15:1: Cn 1018:14:1  VI Atr 22:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="334"><label>recurs in later code</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_22-1">VI Atr 22.1</ref> <quote>Almost all these additions recurred in codes later drafted by Wulfstan for Cnut (n. 332: VI Atr 22.1, Cn 1018 14.1, I Cn 15–15.1)</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 22.1.; Robertson (p. 139) takes I Cn from B, which begins at ‘mæssedæg’ in 14.2, the earlier clauses being supplied from G; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 295, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_15.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dæga <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dæga Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_15.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ge <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ge Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_15.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">296</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_15.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">296</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">myc. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">myc. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_15.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">296</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_15.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">297</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-num <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-num K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_15.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt H</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in H</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_15.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr. Cb</hi>; <hi rend="italic">fehlt H</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above Cb; missing in H</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_15.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">297</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lorum <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lorum Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_15.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">297</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">s. m. <hi rend="italic">HLb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s. m. HLb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_15.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zwischen <hi rend="italic">-daga</hi> und <hi rend="italic">-dæges</hi> schwanken Hss. auch <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 117; <hi rend="italic">-daga</hi> 208. 308, wo im übrigen VI Atr 44, der hier <hi rend="italic">-dæges</hi> hat, benutzt wird</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The MSS vary between <hi rend="italic">-daga</hi> and <hi rend="italic">-dæges</hi> in <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 117 too; <hi rend="italic">-daga</hi> 208. 308, where otherwise VI Atr 44, which has <hi rend="italic">-dæges</hi> here, is used</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_15.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With this clause and the one following, cf. VI Atr. 22, 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_15.robnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope></bibl><label>Sunnandæges</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">-daga</hi> G; <hi rend="italic">-dæga</hi> A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
